# 8. Memory Management

Agent memory should optimize repeated development work without becoming authoritative.

Authority and context hierarchy:

```text
Deployed state / bytecode / version-matched verified source
        ↓
 factual evidence for deployed behavior

Validated registry / canonical knowledge
        ↓
 maintained interpretation and retrieval surface

Derived docs / SDK / skills / examples
        ↓
 consumers; never independent fact owners

Agent memory
        ↓
durable development context

Tasks / reviews
        ↓
implementation history

Session context
        ↓
temporary
```

Repository support:

```text
agents/memory/
├── README.md
├── schema/
├── seed/
└── evals/
```

Useful memory includes:

- accepted development patterns;
- verified Mezo-specific behavior;
- architecture decisions;
- compatibility findings;
- confirmed root causes;
- valuable failed approaches.

Do not use memory for:

- raw logs;
- duplicated source files;
- speculation;
- secrets;
- routine task completion.

Useful discoveries should eventually follow:

```text
discovery
   ↓
memory
   ↓
verification
   ↓
knowledge / ADR / documentation
```

The kit must remain usable without the memory system.

