# 14. Core Client

The framework-independent core provides shared execution infrastructure.

```ts
const client = createMezoClient({
  chain,
  transport,
  registry,
  confirmationPolicy,
});
```

Responsibilities:

```text
transport
chain validation
deployment resolution
block-coherent reads
typed required / optional read failures
provider-aware batching and safe failover
simulation
units
errors
receipt tracking
debug information
```

Chain, transport, registry, and confirmation policy are explicit replaceable
dependencies. Read failover preserves chain identity and the requested block
coordinate. Write failover may rebroadcast identical signed bytes but must not
silently create a second nonce-bearing intent. No external client dependency is
selected by this manifest or ADR-0002.

Protocol packages consume the client:

```ts
const musd = createMusdModule({ client });
```

Framework integrations consume public core/protocol APIs rather than implementing protocol behavior themselves.

