# 16. Tooling Philosophy

The kit should extend existing ecosystem tools rather than replace them.

Expected integrations:

```text
Foundry
Hardhat
viem
wagmi
Scaffold-ETH
```

Mezo-specific tooling should concentrate on repeated Mezo-specific problems:

```text
network configuration
contract metadata
deployment
verification
protocol interactions
debugging
testnet workflows
```

Scaffold-ETH should function as an onboarding layer built on the same underlying packages.

---

# 17. Community Development Model

A small group of contributors should be able to work concurrently around clear ownership boundaries.

Typical areas:

```text
Registry / chain data

Core / protocol SDK

Development tooling

Knowledge / documentation / DX
```

Ownership does not mean isolation.

Public interfaces, architectural changes and protocol-sensitive functionality remain shared review responsibilities.

---

# 18. Guiding Principle

The Mezo Development Kit should not merely contain useful code.

It should contain the **context required to produce correct useful code repeatedly**.

The repository therefore consists of three equally important systems:

```text
             MEZO DEVELOPMENT KIT

                    │
        ┌───────────┼───────────┐
        │           │           │
      CODE       KNOWLEDGE    PROCESS
        │           │           │
     packages       docs       review
     tooling       skills      reviews
     templates     memory      standards
        │           │           │
        └───────────┼───────────┘
                    │
             DEVELOPER EXPERIENCE
```

Code, knowledge and development process should evolve together.
